Package: v4l2-request-va-driver
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: libva2
Description: VA-API driver for V4L2 stateless (Request API) video decoders
 v4l2_request_drv_video.so lets VA-API clients such as ffmpeg, mpv, Qt
 Multimedia and Chromium decode MPEG-2, H.264, HEVC, VP8, VP9 and AV1 on
 the stateless video decoders of the Linux media subsystem (V4L2 Media
 Request API), for example on Rockchip RK3399/RK3588, Allwinner and
 MediaTek SoCs (mtk-vcodec-dec with MM21 block-tiled output).
 .
 libva picks a driver by the name of the DRM driver of the render node. The
 package links panfrost_drv_video.so and panthor_drv_video.so to the driver,
 so it is used without LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME on boards with a Mali GPU.
